From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] propsys: canonical property key names, schema registration, more conversions

- PSGetPropertyKeyFromName was E_NOTIMPL: it now finds a canonical name
  ("System.Photo.CameraModel") in a table of every documented PKEY_*
  (generated from include/propkey.h, dlls/propsys/canonical_propkeys.h),
  case-insensitively, and gives the PROPERTYKEY; an unknown name is
  E_INVALIDARG, a NULL argument E_POINTER.
- PSRegisterPropertySchema and PSUnregisterPropertySchema were FIXME-and-
  succeed / E_NOTIMPL: registering is kept in the registry under
  HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\PropertySystem\
  PropertySchema (again is fine), unregistering something never registered
  is S_FALSE. PSRefreshPropertySchema and the in-memory property store's
  Commit are real no-ops now and no longer FIXME.
- propvar.c: numeric conversion takes VT_R4 and VT_BOOL; PropVariantToBuffer
  copies scalar numeric types, not only VT_VECTOR|VT_UI1; PropVariantToGUID
  parses VT_LPSTR; VariantToGUID parses VT_LPWSTR and VT_BYREF|VT_BSTR;
  VariantToString falls back to VariantChangeType for every type without a
  hand-written case (so VT_EMPTY is "", and the todo_wine in the propsys
  test for it is gone).
- propsys now imports advapi32 for the schema registry calls.

Gate: test/propkeyname-gate.sh (test/propkeyname-probe.c). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_PROPKEYFROMNAME, SG_MUTANT_SCHEMAREG, SG_MUTANT_CONVERTNUMBER,
SG_MUTANT_PROPVARTOBUFFER, SG_MUTANT_VARIANTTOGUID,
SG_MUTANT_VARIANTTOSTRING each fail it. Wine's propsys test: 801 tests,
0 failures (one todo_wine now passes and is removed).
---
--- a/dlls/propsys/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/propsys/Makefile.in
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 EXTRADEFS = -D_PROPSYS_
 MODULE    = propsys.dll
 IMPORTLIB = propsys
-IMPORTS   = ole32 oleaut32 uuid
+IMPORTS   = advapi32 ole32 oleaut32 uuid
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
 
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/propsys/canonical_propkeys.h
@@ -0,0 +1,1082 @@
